com/godotengine/godot/pull/99456.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This is a very, very, VERY work-in-progress means of detecting a header's `#include` files & ensuring that they aren't breaking the \"\"\"expected\"\"\" dependency order. Right now, said order is barely a suggestion, but consequences are rare as things function anyway 99% of the time. Even so, that makes diagnosing those issues a pain in the ass that 1% of the time, often leading to us realizing that we've been building our house of cards upside-down all this time.\r\n\r\nThis PR is a starting point in identifying rudamentary areas where these conventions are broken. A hell of a lot of these are probably false positives, and I certainly didn't setup everything correctly to begin with—it was made less with the expectation of being merged, and more with the intent to highlight dependencies as they currently exist.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99456/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99456/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}